#: {{ux|en|'''Reference''' the dictionary for word meanings.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1990|author=Thomas L. Bell|title=Political Economy's Response to Positivism|journal=w:Geographical Review|volume=80|number=3|jstor=215307|publisher=American Geographical Society|page=314|passage=The penchant for synthesizing the work of others that pervades British scholarship has been described by one of my cynical American colleagues as “a giant bibliography that is always eating its own tail.” By this he means that cliques of like-minded writers tend to '''reference''' each other’s work incessantly.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1994-09|author=Barry Chamish|quotee=Louis Rossetto<!-- the article is inconsistent with one vs. two ‘S’s, but the correct spelling is with two -->|title=The End of the Book|journal=w:The Atlantic|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/1994/09/the-end-of-the-book/376361/|passage=Written information is a relatively new phenomenon. Depositing it and being able to '''reference''' it centuries later is not common human experience.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250903170010/https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/1994/09/the-end-of-the-book/376361/|archivedate=3 September 2025}}
#* {{RQ:WaPo|date=1998-01-26|author=Donnie Radcliffe|title=New Library Will Chronicle First Ladies|pages=C1+|passage=On the Florence Harding page, for instance, a researcher will be able to '''reference''' a book by Waarren Harding’s alleged mistress, Nan Britton, who claimed that she bore his daughter.}}
# {{lb|en|sometimes|proscribed}} To [[mention]], to [[refer]] to.
#: {{ux|en|In his speech, the candidate obliquely '''referenced''' the past failures of his opponent.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1988|title=Integrating the Humanities into Associate Degree Occupational Programs|publisher=w:American Association of Community Colleges|isbn=0-87117-192-9|page=25|passage=Humanities institutions specifically '''reference''' the work setting for illustrative applications of the unique and significant contributions of the Humanities.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1990|author=Jean Borgatti|title=Portraiture in Africa|journal=[[w:African Arts (journal)|African Arts]]|volume=23|number=3|page=37|passage=With the economy characteristic of all African sculpture, these portraits '''reference''' individual and social identities simultaneously, so that the image of a king may represent a particular king and all kings; a commemorative mask for a woman, a particular woman and all titled women.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=1991-01-19|author=w:Bobby Ray Inman|title=A Nominee’s Withdrawal: Transcript of the Statement by Inman on His Decision to Withdraw|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1994/01/19/us/nominee-s-withdrawal-transcript-statement-inman-his-decision-withdraw.html|page=A14|pageurl=https://timesmachine.nytimes.com/timesmachine/1994/01/19/914592.html|passage=And I would simply '''reference''' those of you who are out there working.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250903135024/https://www.nytimes.com/1994/01/19/us/nominee-s-withdrawal-transcript-statement-inman-his-decision-withdraw.html|archivedate=3 September 2025}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Kaitlan Collins, Samantha Waldenberg and Tierney Sneed|title=Trump involved in discussions over suspending habeas corpus, sources say|url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/05/09/politics/miller-habeas-corpus-immigrant-judge|date=2025-05-09|passage=While Trump has not explicitly mentioned habeas corpus in public, it’s what he was '''referencing''' last month when he commented on steps he could take to combat nationwide injunctions against his actions on deportations, according to one of the people familiar with the talks.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260218140511/https://www.cnn.com/2025/05/09/politics/miller-habeas-corpus-immigrant-judge|archivedate=18 February 2026}}
